2. Sentiment Analysis
Definition

Sentiment Analysis is the process of identifying the emotional tone, opinion, or feeling expressed in a piece of text.

It generally classifies text into three categories:

Types of Sentiment

✅ Positive

Example:

"I love this product."

✅ Negative

Example:

"The product is damaged."

✅ Neutral

Example:

"Product received yesterday."

Application in UiPath

After analyzing customer reviews, UiPath can:

Store positive reviews in Excel.
Send negative reviews to customer support.
Maintain neutral reviews for analysis.
---------------------------------------------------------
Machine Learning (ML)
Definition

Machine Learning (ML) is a branch of Artificial Intelligence that enables 
computers to learn patterns from data and make predictions without being explicitly programmed for every condition.

Example

Instead of creating hundreds of rules to identify positive and negative reviews,
a trained ML model can automatically predict the sentiment.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. ML Skills in UiPath
Definition

An ML Skill in UiPath is a deployed Machine Learning model that can be used inside UiPath automation workflows.

Purpose

ML Skills allow UiPath robots to:

Analyze text
Classify documents
Detect languages
Predict sentiments
Make intelligent decisions
Example

Customer Review:

"The product quality is excellent."

Sentiment Analysis ML Skill → Positive

UiPath then stores the review automatically.
